    note right of DELETED
        Base removal requires the owning authenticated Actor context.
        Binding release and Source audit intent commit together.
        Exact terminal retry creates no further intent.
        Settings replacement retains old status and releases its binding fact
        atomically with the new candidate and both Source intents.
        Signup Ticket failure preserves the committed binding and original audit intent.
        Exact bound checkpoint reconciliation rewrites neither fact.
        Database binding checks reject null, empty and whitespace-only digests.
        Forward recognition requires Source intent or completed signup proof.
        Unknown history or effective conflicts abort with row IDs.
        Existing facts, status and OTP counters remain unchanged.
    end note
